63 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 48 0 R
/T (This report presents findings from a focus group in Rochdale in which eight young South Asian men discussed addiction, family life, faith and the response of local institutions. They described changing patterns of drug use, including large nitrous oxide canisters, discreet vaping, cannabis products resembling sweets and dealing through private social-media accounts.)
/E (This report presents findings from a focus group in Rochdale in which eight young South Asian men discussed addiction, family life, faith and the response of local institutions. They described changing patterns of drug use, including large nitrous oxide canisters, discreet vaping, cannabis products resembling sweets and dealing through private social-media accounts.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
64 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 48 0 R
/T (The conversation moved beyond individual substances. Participants considered why people begin using drugs, why others stay away, how punishment and shame affect disclosure, and what families, schools, mosques and services could do differently. Their contributions showed considerable awareness, concern and a clear desire for earlier, more honest and more consistent action.)
/E (The conversation moved beyond individual substances. Participants considered why people begin using drugs, why others stay away, how punishment and shame affect disclosure, and what families, schools, mosques and services could do differently. Their contributions showed considerable awareness, concern and a clear desire for earlier, more honest and more consistent action.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
