99 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 49 0 R
/E (Participants did not agree on a single definition of addiction. Most believed that trying a substance may begin as a choice, but repeated use can develop into dependency and make stopping increasingly difficult. Some emphasised personal responsibility and willpower, noting that people exposed to the same pressures do not always make the same decisions. Others focused more on environment, peer influence and the normalisation of drug use within friendship groups and neighbourhoods.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
