/P 50 0 R
/E (The mosque occupied a complicated but important place in the discussion. Participants recognised that some mosques and imams were willing to address addiction and social problems, while others lacked the knowledge, confidence or resources to respond. They also distinguished between the compassion taught by faith and cultural attitudes that could drive struggling people away.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
131 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 50 0 R
/E (One participant recalled an elder publicly challenging a young man for wearing an earring when he entered the mosque. The embarrassment caused him to leave. Participants felt that welcoming him, allowing him to pray and then speaking to him privately would have been more compassionate and more likely to keep him connected.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 50 0 R
