/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (Participants believed that responsibility was shared. Government and police had a role in addressing the supply of drugs, but families, schools, mosques, recovery services and community organisations also had a part to play in prevention and support.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
161 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (They were also frustrated by consultations that appeared to produce no visible action. Communities could become disheartened when they were repeatedly asked to discuss the same problems without being told what changed as a result. Listening must therefore be followed by action, continued contact and honest feedback about what can and cannot be done.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
