/Title (This report presents findings from a focus group in Rochdale in which eight young South Asian men discussed addiction, family life, faith and the response of local institutions. They described changing patterns of drug use, including large nitrous oxide canisters, discreet vaping, cannabis products resembling sweets and dealing through private social-media accounts.)
